# Solarus runtime flag OVERRIDES — sourced by solarus_run.sh whenever this file
# EXISTS (the old second key, SOLARUS_ALLOW_DIAG_ENV=1, was removed 2026-07-19).
# End-user protection is now by ABSENCE: deploy.py removes this file on every
# deploy UNLESS run with --diag. To force it off without deleting it, launch with
# SOLARUS_NO_DIAG_ENV=1.
#
# *** PRECEDENCE WARNING ***
# solarus_run.sh sources this file with `set -a`, so every assignment here
# OVERRIDES the launch environment. A variable you intend to vary per-leg of an
# A/B must NOT be assigned in this file, or both legs silently measure the same
# path. That is why SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB is deliberately absent below.
#
# HW-validated perf/correctness levers are ENGINE DEFAULTS (ON without any env var):
# SOLARUS_TILERESIDENT (#56), SOLARUS_FASTPACE (#54/55), SOLARUS_AUDIO_THREAD (#55),
# SOLARUS_IDLEPARK (#59), SOLARUS_BGPLANE (#121), SOLARUS_OVERLAY (#125).

# ===========================================================================
# STAGE 3a — scroll-transition fabric path: #122 / #123 A/B session
# ===========================================================================
#
# *** DEFAULTS CHANGED 2026-07-20 (commit 861c792) — re-read before reusing this. ***
# SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB and SOLARUS_SPRITECH are now ENGINE DEFAULTS (ON), and
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE is now default OFF. Consequences for any future A/B here:
#   - To get a SCROLLFAB baseline you must now inject =0 explicitly; "unset" is no
#     longer the baseline, it is the new path.
#   - The SPRITECH=1 line below is now redundant with the default. Harmless, but it
#     no longer "pins" anything the engine would not do anyway.
#   - The bake is OFF unless you set SOLARUS_BGPLANE=1. It was turned off because it
#     causes the scroll seam to render the incoming map as plain background_color
#     (#122), the transition hitch + flash (#127), and probably the scroll black
#     frame (#123). Stage 3b deletes it. Set =1 only to reproduce those defects.
# Session record: docs/superpowers/2026-07-20-stage3a-hw-validation.md

SOLARUS_BLITTER_DIAG=1     # per-60fr [blitter*] banners -> /media/fat/logs/Solarus/Solarus.diag.log
SOLARUS_SPRITECH=1         # HELD CONSTANT ACROSS BOTH LEGS — see note below

# SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB is INTENTIONALLY NOT SET HERE. It is the variable under test.
# Inject it per leg in the launch environment:
#     leg A (baseline, software scroll):  SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB=0
#     leg B (fabric scroll):              SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB=1
# The launcher echoes the flags in effect — confirm leg B prints
#     [MiSTer blitter] scroll fabric path ENABLED (SOLARUS_SCROLLFAB)
# before collecting any data. Without that line the leg measured the default path.

# Why SPRITECH is pinned ON for both legs rather than left off:
# it was HW-validated in Stage 2 (~16k frames, 218k sprites, operator confirmed the
# sprites render correctly), and leg B's old-map branch calls
# flush_sprites_before_other_op() — a fix that is only exercised with SPRITECH on.
# Holding it constant keeps it out of the comparison while still testing the real
# configuration. Set it =0 in BOTH legs if you want it out of the picture entirely.

# --- HOW TO RUN THIS SESSION ---------------------------------------------
# 1. SCROLL ALL FOUR DIRECTIONS. Stage 3a added a destination-side clip for the
#    bgplane plane COPY whose ddx<0 / ddy<0 branches fire on only ONE direction per
#    axis. Those branches are the only genuinely new logic on the branch, and they
#    guard against a negative destination wrapping through blt_blit's uint16_t
#    fields (the #24 out-of-bounds class). A one-direction A/B leaves them cold.
# 2. RESTART solarus-run BETWEEN LEGS. heap_peak is a monotonic high-water mark for
#    the process lifetime and is deliberately NOT reset per window. In one process
#    leg B can only ever read >= leg A and a real reduction is invisible. Discard
#    the first post-boot peak — that is warm-up, not transition, allocation.
# 3. THE TITLE SCREEN CANNOT TEST #122/#123. With no previous map
#    g_transition_scroll is never true, and with no tile layers the bgplane hold
#    frame is structurally impossible. A clean title screen proves nothing.
#    Use an overworld map edge: map 8 to_B1 -> map 9, to_A2 -> map 10;
#    map 9 to_C1 -> map 3. Simplest repro is walking off a screen edge.
# 4. No RTL changed in Stage 3a, so Solarus_20260719.rbf is correct — but CONFIRM
#    which core is loaded. The older RBF still on the device has no arm for opcode
#    10 and renders visible garbage that looks like an engine bug.

# --- WHAT TO READ OUT OF Solarus.diag.log --------------------------------
# [blitter diag]
#   scroll_off=(ndx,ndy)/(odx,ody)  engine-truth scroll offsets, INSTANTANEOUS
#                 (not windowed). These must ANIMATE across a transition. Stuck at
#                 (0,0) during a scroll localizes the failure to the ENGINE HOOK
#                 (series patch 0040), not the renderer.
#   scroll_oldmap= old-map blits emitted to the fabric (leg B only; 0 in leg A)
#   scroll_oldclip= old-map blits that were FULLY CLIPPED and drew nothing.
#                 Should sit at/near ZERO through a normal transition, with at most
#                 a small tail on the final frames as the old map leaves screen.
#                 A LARGE count means the offsets are wrong in the other direction.
#                 Do not read "scroll_oldmap is nonzero" as success on its own.
#   heap_peak=    DDR bounce-heap HIGH-WATER, monotonic per process. This is the
#                 ONLY signal that speaks to #123's heap premise.
#                 *** Do NOT cite the [blitter inter] line for any heap claim —
#                 that reads the SDRAM INTER arena, a DIFFERENT region. ***
#   overflow= / dropped=  must both be 0.
#
# --- INTERPRETATION RULES (settled by code review, do not re-derive) ------
# * An UNDER-DIMMED scroll frame is a REAL defect (#122/#123/#124). It is NOT a
#   Stage 3a double-composite: Task 6 established by control-flow proof that no
#   redundant overlay composite is reachable with SCROLLFAB on.
# * OLD-MAP CONTENT OVER NEW-MAP SPRITES AT THE SEAM would mean the disjoint-rect
#   invariant has broken (the two maps are assumed to occupy adjacent,
#   non-overlapping camera-sized rects).
# * A PERSISTENTLY SHIFTED FRAME AFTER a transition ends = stale scroll state from
#   tearing the game down mid-transition. Known, flag-ON only, self-evident.

# --- other diagnostics (extra perf cost + log spam) -----------------------
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE_DIAG=1     # per-bake ARM/BAKE/EMIT census (needs BGPLANE on)

# --- opt-outs (uncomment to disable a HW-validated default for an A/B) ----
# SOLARUS_OVERLAY=0          # force the overlay channel OFF
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE=0          # force the per-layer plane bake OFF
# SOLARUS_BGPLANE_SYNC=0     # legacy one-cell-per-frame bake (default is synchronous load-time)
# SOLARUS_TILERESIDENT=0
# SOLARUS_FASTPACE=0
# SOLARUS_AUDIO_THREAD=0
# SOLARUS_IDLEPARK=0
